Hello out there-

Well, whoever it was that asked a load of questions, here are some of the
answers.

(****Spoiler alert****)





















To keep track of time:  use the time option (in the options menu).  This 
   adds a turn number display to your status line.

About magic lamps:  Luck has something to do with the wish ratio for these,
   but the best idea is still to get it blessed somehow.  Blessed magic lamps
   *always* give wishes.

If anyone knows what the chill running up your arm from fountains is, I would
   also like to know.  I knew once, but have forgotten.

"You feel healthy" means that you have poison resistance, while
   "You feel a momentary chill" means heat resistance.

I don't know about aquired pets (I don't think it works with them), but
   your starting pets, even if polymorphed, won't step on a cursed item until
   the prohibition against this is broken.  The only way I know of to do this
   is to put food in the same square as the cursed item.  Then, however, the
   pet will even pick up cursed items!

Cursed and blessed wands function no differently from ordinary wands.

Blessed spellbooks are always successfully memorized.  I don't know what
   cursed ones do.

Some rings are enhanced by blessedness.  (Of course you know what curses do
   to rings...;-\ )

To name items you use the #name command.  It asks, I believe, which type of
   naming you want to do.  Or at least, it does in Patch 5.

There is a luck penalty for killing, eating, or abandoning your original pet
   on a level.  As for others, your guess is as good as mine.

Oh, yes, there are two ways besides the ways you mentioned to uncurse an
   object.  One is dipping it in a fountain (this can be risky unless your
   luck is good).  The other is prayer;  sometimes the gods will uncurse 
   everrything in your backpack.

